<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Learn Python 🐍</title>

    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f4f7fb;
            color: #222;
        }

        header {
            background: #306998;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 35px 20px;
        }

        header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 42px;
        }

        header p {
            font-size: 18px;
        }

        nav {
            background: #ffd43b;
            padding: 12px;
            text-align: center;
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
        }

        nav a {
            color: #222;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin: 0 15px;
        }

        nav a:hover {
            color: #306998;
        }

        main {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: auto;
            padding: 25px;
        }

        section {
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
        }

        h2 {
            color: #306998;
        }

        h3 {
            color: #444;
        }

        code {
            display: block;
            background: #222;
            color: #00ff88;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-family: Consolas, monospace;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }

        .tip {
            background: #fff3cd;
            border-left: 5px solid #ffd43b;
            padding: 12px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        button {
            background: #306998;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 12px 20px;
            border-radius: 7px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        button:hover {
            background: #24527a;
        }

        .question {
            margin-bottom: 25px;
        }

        #result {
            font-size: 20px;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        footer {
            background: #306998;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>🐍 Learn Python</h1>
        <p>A beginner-friendly guide to Python programming</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="#basics">Basics</a>
        <a href="#variables">Variables</a>
        <a href="#if">If Statements</a>
        <a href="#quiz">Quiz</a>
    </nav>

    <main>

        <!-- ABOUT -->
        <section id="about">
            <h2>🐍 What is Python?</h2>

            <p>
                Python is a programming language used to tell computers
                what to do. It is popular because its code is relatively
                easy for beginners to read and write.
            </p>

            <p>
                Python can be used to create websites, programs,
                data projects, artificial intelligence and much more.
            </p>

            <div class="tip">
                💡 Tip: Programming is about giving a computer instructions
                in a language it can understand.
            </div>
        </section>


        <!-- BASICS -->
        <section id="basics">
            <h2>📚 Lesson 1: The print() Function</h2>

            <p>
                The <strong>print()</strong> function tells Python to
                display something on the screen.
            </p>

            <code>
print("Hello, world!")
            </code>

            <p>This would display:</p>

            <code>
Hello, world!
            </code>

            <h3>Try another example:</h3>

            <code>
print("I am learning Python!")<br>
print("Python is fun!")
            </code>
        </section>


        <!-- VARIABLES -->
        <section id="variables">
            <h2>📦 Lesson 2: Variables</h2>

            <p>
                A variable is like a box that stores information.
            </p>

            <code>
name = "Alex"<br>
age = 12
            </code>

            <p>
                The variable <strong>name</strong> stores "Alex", while
                <strong>age</strong> stores the number 12.
            </p>

            <code>
name = "Alex"<br>
print(name)
            </code>

            <p>The result would be:</p>

            <code>
Alex
            </code>
        </section>


        <!-- INPUT -->
        <section>
            <h2>⌨️ Lesson 3: User Input</h2>

            <p>
                Python can ask the user for information using
                <strong>input()</strong>.
            </p>

            <code>
name = input("What is your name?")<br>
print("Hello " + name)
            </code>

            <p>
                If the user enters <strong>Sam</strong>, the program
                will say:
            </p>

            <code>
Hello Sam
            </code>
        </section>


        <!-- IF STATEMENTS -->
        <section id="if">
            <h2>🔀 Lesson 4: If Statements</h2>

            <p>
                An <strong>if statement</strong> allows Python to make
                decisions.
            </p>

            <code>
age = 12<br><br>

if age >= 10:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print("You are 10 or older!")
            </code>

            <p>
                Python checks whether the condition is true.
                If it is true, the indented code runs.
            </p>

            <div class="tip">
                💡 Remember: Python uses indentation to show which
                instructions belong inside an if statement.
            </div>
        </section>


        <!-- LOOPS -->
        <section>
            <h2>🔁 Lesson 5: Loops</h2>

            <p>
                Loops allow you to repeat instructions.
            </p>

            <code>
for i in range(5):<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print("Hello!")
            </code>

            <p>
                This prints "Hello!" five times.
            </p>
        </section>


        <!-- QUIZ -->
        <section id="quiz">
            <h2>📝 Python Quiz</h2>

            <div class="question">
                <p><strong>1. What does print() do?</strong></p>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q1" value="wrong">
                    Deletes information
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q1" value="correct">
                    Displays something on the screen
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q1" value="wrong">
                    Turns off Python
                </label>
            </div>


            <div class="question">
                <p><strong>2. What is a variable?</strong></p>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q2" value="correct">
                    A place that stores information
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q2" value="wrong">
                    A computer screen
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q2" value="wrong">
                    A type of keyboard
                </label>
            </div>


            <div class="question">
                <p><strong>3. Which function gets information from the user?</strong></p>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q3" value="wrong">
                    print()
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q3" value="correct">
                    input()
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q3" value="wrong">
                    ask()
                </label>
            </div>


            <div class="question">
                <p><strong>4. What can a loop do?</strong></p>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q4" value="correct">
                    Repeat instructions
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q4" value="wrong">
                    Delete Python
                </label><br>

                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="q4" value="wrong">
                    Change your computer
                </label>
            </div>


            <button onclick="checkQuiz()">Check My Answers</button>

            <p id="result"></p>
        </section>

    </main>


    <footer>
        <p>🐍 Learn Python | Made for beginner programmers</p>
    </footer>


    <script>
        function checkQuiz() {

            let questions = document.querySelectorAll(
                'input[type="radio"]:checked'
            );

            let score = 0;

            questions.forEach(function(answer) {

                if (answer.value === "correct") {
                    score++;
                }

            });

            let result = document.getElementById("result");

            if (questions.length < 4) {
                result.textContent =
                    "Please answer all 4 questions!";
                result.style.color = "orange";
            }

            else {
                result.textContent =
                    "You scored " + score + " out of 4! 🎉";

                if (score === 4) {
                    result.style.color = "green";
                }

                else {
                    result.style.color = "#306998";
                }
            }
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
